One article is added after Article 134 of the Criminal Law as Article 134-1: "Whoever, in the course of production or operation, violates the provisions on safety management, in any of the following circumstances, thereby creating a real danger of a major accident involving serious casualties or other serious consequences, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than one year, criminal detention or public surveillance:
(1) shutting down or destroying monitoring, alarm, protection, or life-saving equipment or facilities directly related to production safety, or tampering with, concealing, or destroying their relevant data or information;
(2) where, due to the existence of major accident hazards, ordered according to law to suspend production or business, stop construction, stop using relevant equipment, facilities, or places, or immediately take corrective measures to eliminate dangers, but refuses to implement such orders;
(3) without obtaining the approval or permission required by law for matters involving production safety, engaging in highly dangerous production or operation activities such as mining, metal smelting, building construction, and the production, operation, or storage of dangerous goods."

One article is added after Article 142 of the Criminal Law as Article 142-1: "Whoever, in violation of drug administrative regulations, in any of the following circumstances, where it is sufficient to seriously endanger human health, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if it causes serious harm to human health or if there are other serious circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) producing or selling drugs that are prohibited from use by the drug regulatory department of the State Council;
(2) producing or importing drugs without obtaining the relevant drug approval certificates, or selling such drugs knowing them to be such;
(3) in the drug registration application, providing false certificates, data, materials, samples, or adopting other deceptive means;
(4) fabricating production or inspection records.
Where an act described in the preceding paragraph simultaneously constitutes a crime under Article 141 or Article 142 of this Law or any other crime, the offender shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions for the heavier punishment."

Paragraph 1 of Article 182 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, in any of the following circumstances, manipulates the securities or futures market, affecting the price or volume of securities or futures trading, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are especially serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined:
(1) alone or in collusion, concentrating capital advantages, shareholding or position advantages, or using information advantages, jointly or continuously trading;
(2) colluding with another person to conduct securities or futures transactions between each other at a predetermined time, price, or manner;
(3) conducting securities transactions between accounts under his own actual control, or trading futures contracts with himself as the counterparty;
(4) frequently or largely placing orders to buy or sell securities or futures contracts and canceling the orders without the intent to execute the transactions;
(5) using false or uncertain material information to induce investors to conduct securities or futures transactions;
(6) publicly making evaluations, forecasts, or investment recommendations on securities, securities issuers, or futures trading targets while simultaneously conducting reverse securities transactions or related futures transactions;
(7) manipulating the securities or futures market by other methods."

Article 191 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, for the purpose of concealing or disguising the source and nature of the proceeds obtained from crimes of drug trafficking, organized crimes of a mafia-like nature, terrorist activities, smuggling, embezzlement or bribery, disrupting the order of financial management, or financial fraud, and the gains derived therefrom, commits any of the following acts, the proceeds obtained from the above crimes and the gains derived therefrom shall be confiscated, and the offender shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined:
(1) providing a fund account;
(2) converting property into cash, financial instruments, or negotiable securities;
(3) transferring funds through transfer or other payment settlement methods;
(4) cross-border transfer of assets;
(5) concealing or disguising the source and nature of the proceeds and gains from crimes by other methods.
Where a unit commits the crime described in the preceding paragraph, the unit shall be fined, and the directly responsible supervisor and other directly liable personnel shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph."

Article 217 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, for the purpose of profit, commits any of the following acts infringing upon copyright or rights related to copyright, where the amount of illegal gains is relatively large or there are other serious circumstances, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years and shall also, or shall only, be fined; where the amount of illegal gains is huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined:
(1) without the permission of the copyright owner, reproducing, distributing, or communicating to the public through information networks his written works, music, fine arts, audiovisual works, computer software, or other works as provided for by laws and administrative regulations;
(2) publishing a book for which another person has exclusive publishing rights;
(3) without the permission of the sound recording or video recording producer, reproducing, distributing, or communicating to the public through information networks the sound recordings or video recordings produced by him;
(4) without the permission of the performer, reproducing, distributing, or communicating to the public through information networks the sound recordings or video recordings containing his performance;
(5) producing or selling fine arts works with a false signature of another person;
(6) without the permission of the copyright owner or the owner of rights related to copyright, intentionally circumventing or destroying the technological measures taken by the right owner to protect his copyright or rights related to copyright for his works, sound recordings, or video recordings."

Article 219 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Any person who commits any of the following acts infringing on a trade secret, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are especially serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined:
(1) obtaining the right holder's trade secret by theft, bribery, fraud, coercion, electronic intrusion, or any other improper means;
(2) disclosing, using, or allowing another person to use the trade secret obtained by the means described in the preceding item;
(3) disclosing, using, or allowing another person to use the trade secret in his possession, in breach of the confidentiality obligation or the right holder's requirements for keeping the trade secret confidential.
Any person who knows the acts listed in the preceding paragraph but still obtains, discloses, uses, or allows another person to use the trade secret shall be deemed to have infringed on the trade secret.
The "right holder" referred to in this Article means the owner of the trade secret and the user of the trade secret authorized by the owner."

Article 229 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Where personnel of an intermediary organization that assumes responsibilities such as asset valuation, capital verification, verification, accounting, auditing, legal services, sponsorship, safety assessment, environmental impact assessment, or environmental monitoring intentionally provide false certification documents, if the circumstances are serious, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention and shall also be fined; in any of the following circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined:
(1) providing false certification documents relating to the issuance of securities, such as asset valuation, accounting, auditing, legal services, or sponsorship, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(2) providing false certification documents relating to major asset transactions, such as asset valuation, accounting, or auditing, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(3) providing false safety assessment, environmental impact assessment, or other certification documents in major projects or programs involving public safety, thereby causing particularly heavy losses to public property or the interests of the State and the people.
Where a person who commits an act described in the preceding paragraph also demands or illegally accepts property from another person, constituting a crime, he shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions for the heavier punishment.
Where the personnel specified in the first paragraph, due to gross negligence, issue certification documents that are materially inaccurate, causing serious consequences, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined."

Article 236 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever rapes a woman by violence, coercion, or any other means shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years.
Whoever has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of fourteen shall be deemed to have committed rape and shall be given a severe punishment.
Whoever rapes a woman or has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of fourteen, in any of the following circumstances, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years, life imprisonment, or death:
(1) the circumstances of rape or sexual intercourse are flagrant;
(2) raping multiple women or having sexual intercourse with multiple girls under the age of fourteen;
(3) raping a woman or having sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of fourteen in a public place in the presence of others;
(4) gang rape by two or more persons;
(5) having sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of ten or causing injury to the girl;
(6) causing serious injury or death to the victim, or causing other serious consequences."

Paragraph 3 of Article 237 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever indecently assaults a child shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years; in any of the following circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years:
(1) indecently assaulting multiple children or indecently assaulting a child multiple times;
(2) gathering people to indecently assault a child, or indecently assaulting a child in a public place in the presence of others, where the circumstances are flagrant;
(3) causing injury to the child or other serious consequences;
(4) the means of indecent assault are vile or there are other vile circumstances."

One article is added after Article 293 of the Criminal Law as Article 293-1: "Whoever, in any of the following circumstances, collects illegal debts arising from high-interest lending or the like, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance and shall also, or shall only, be fined:
(1) using violence or coercion;
(2) restricting the personal freedom of another person or intruding into another person's residence;
(3) intimidating, stalking, or harassing another person."

Paragraph 1 of Article 330 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, in violation of the provisions of the Law on the Prevention and Control of Infectious Diseases, in any of the following circumstances, causes the spread of a Class A infectious disease or an infectious disease for which prevention and control measures applicable to Class A infectious diseases are determined according to law, or creates a serious risk of such spread, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention; if the consequences are especially serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years:
(1) the drinking water supplied by a water supply unit does not meet the hygienic standards prescribed by the State;
(2) refusing to disinfect sewage, waste, premises, or articles contaminated by the pathogens of an infectious disease in accordance with the hygienic requirements put forward by the disease prevention and control institution;
(3) permitting or conniving at the engagement of persons suffering from an infectious disease, pathogen carriers, or persons suspected of suffering from an infectious disease in work that is prohibited by the health administrative department of the State Council because it is likely to cause the spread of the infectious disease;
(4) selling or transporting articles that are or may be contaminated by the pathogens of an infectious disease in an epidemic area without carrying out disinfection;
(5) refusing to implement the preventive and control measures proposed by the people's government at or above the county level or the disease prevention and control institution in accordance with the Law on the Prevention and Control of Infectious Diseases."

Article 338 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Whoever, in violation of State regulations, discharges, dumps, or disposes of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances, or other harmful substances, thereby seriously polluting the environment, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined; in any of the following circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances in drinking water source protection areas, core protection areas of nature reserves, or other key protection areas determined according to law, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(2) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances into the waters of major rivers or lakes designated by the State, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(3) causing a large area of permanent basic farmland to lose its basic function or suffer permanent damage;
(4) causing multiple persons to suffer serious injury, serious illness, or causing serious disability or death.
Where an act described in the preceding paragraph simultaneously constitutes another crime, the offender shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions for the heavier punishment."

Paragraph 1 of Article 408-1 of the Criminal Law is amended as: "Where a State functionary who is responsible for the supervision and administration of food and drug safety abuses his power or neglects his duties, in any of the following circumstances, causing serious consequences or having other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention; if particularly serious consequences are caused or there are other particularly serious circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years:
(1) concealing or falsely reporting food safety accidents or drug safety incidents;
(2) failing to investigate and deal with serious illegal acts concerning food and drug safety that have been discovered in accordance with regulations;
(3) granting permits to applications that do not meet the conditions in the process of approving and reviewing drugs and special foods;
(4) failing to transfer cases that should be transferred to the judicial authorities for criminal liability according to law;
(5) other acts of abusing power or neglecting duties."
